## Where things are
| Need | Go to |
|---|---|
| Game code | `src/server`, `src/client`, `src/shared` (Rojo: `default.project.json`) |
| Factory packages (scene authoring, procedural generation, import checks) | `packages/`, synced to `ReplicatedStorage.Workbench` |
| Specs | `tests/*.spec.luau`, run by `lune run tests/run.luau` |
| Gate | `python3 tools/check.py [--tier fast] [--strict]` |
| Skills | `.agents/skills/` (Codex), mirrored to `.claude/skills/` by `python3 tools/sync_skills.py` |
| Decisions | `docs/decisions.md` |

## Factory packages and references
- `packages/` are copies of the factory's packages. Fix package bugs in the factory, then pull them here: on a clean branch, run the factory's `python3 tools/new_project.py --update <this repo>` and review `git diff`. It refuses when a package was edited here (its hash no longer matches `starter.json`).
- The copied skills also name factory-only paths (`tools/blender/`, `tools/lune/`, `fixtures/`, `docs/`, `knowledge/`). Those live in the factory repository at the commit in `starter.json`; do Blender asset and research work there. Where a skill says `fixtures/factory.project.json`, use `default.project.json` here.

## Working rules
- Read the skill for the task, not the whole repo. Retrieve with `rg`.
- New Luau logic gets a Lune spec in `tests/`. Never skip or weaken a test or validation rule to get green.
- Before committing: `python3 tools/check.py`. CI runs it with `--strict`.
- One writer per Studio session and per file set.

## Verification language
VERIFIED_STRONG, VERIFIED_ACCEPTABLE, WEAK, PARTIAL, BROKEN, MISSING, OUTDATED, REDUNDANT, BLOCKED_EXTERNAL, INTENTIONALLY_EXCLUDED. Verified means a representative execution produced observed output. Files, docs, configs or screenshots alone are not verification.
